{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact 5a15b9b02dd7889420548b83fa75a3625f20ad61 on request/scope-contract-r15, under promise git:sha1…57165ef on request git:sha1…f2c7bab\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 17 at 5a15b9b02dd7889420548b83fa75a3625f20ad61 on request/scope-contract-r15 (one commit on adopted revision 16, 54420b41), for request 9626787f. All four subjects; the two companions are unchanged. The canonical URI, new section 3.1: artroom://host[:port]/\u003cscope\u003e[\u003cfact tail\u003e | \u003citem tail\u003e], where a scope is sc_ and 52 lowercase base32 characters with an optional @in_ and 26 more; a fact tail is /\u003cseq\u003e/sha256:\u003c64 lowercase hex\u003e; an item tail is /items/\u003ctype\u003e/\u003cn\u003e; no user information, query or fragment. Normal form: lower-case scheme and host, non-ASCII host labels as A-labels, port 443 dropped, one trailing slash removed; an ID or hash with an upper-case letter is refused, not folded. Three relations are told apart: identical, same scope ID whatever the host, and same reference, which needs both incarnations present and equal or a fact's hash. A fact URI is self-verifying whatever host answers. Mapping to the https read routes: the scope and fact routes exist; reading by incarnation and the one-item route do not and are source rows. A host with no copy answers not-found, which says nothing of other hosts; a reader must not trust a host for the head or for being the ordering place; redirects only to https and with no credential; a URI carries no authority and no secret. A label owner/repository#number is not a URI and not an identity: it resolves by two reads to a scope URI; neither read has a route yet. A URI presents a reference and is not a fifth class; no entry holds one. Bounds of 253 bytes for a host and 2,048 for a URI are proposals for the proof plan. Also in this revision, the questions the platform-marks source raised (I3 deltas EJ1 to EJ15), each answered: an outcome's mark may hold one send, and the creation cause for a scope created by an outcome entry already exists as the fourth cause; where the membership reference is recorded; a clause does not run an also mark's rule again; at most one mark per written send list; a rule's refusals, most and clock are members of the mark and the validator counts the most; a grant rule passes with no member. Source rows I3-17 to I3-26 are added. Reading limits, stated in the note: the EJ answers rest on the I3 deltas note and not on a reading of the judges or the validator; the URI grammar follows the URI standards from memory, not a parser; single writer. Read with the authority note's revision 22, filed with it. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"5a15b9b02dd7889420548b83fa75a3625f20ad61","path":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md"}}